= Basic =
alias Question to Q
alias Answer to A

(Q) What is the most basic of regular expressions?
(A) The single literal character, which matches the first occurence of it in a string.

(Q) By default, regex engines match how many times?
(A) Once, the first. But for convenience, many iterate through every match.

(Q) How to match unicode characters if it's not supported in the syntax?
(A) Use \xFF to match a character by its hexadecimal index in the character set.

